{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"32a93d593c1992b556b3bac42ba9921cccbf1fee"},"timestamp":1511800474,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzcwODM5NTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1997","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad add-archive-content: better documentation","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\n1. I have no clue on how to use `datalad add-archive-content`, and the error message/documentation could be more informative.\n~~2. It fails to add the content of the archive under git annex.~~ (dumb me I had `.gitignore` set to ignore the files that were in the tar)\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n\nI have a tarball, which is untracked. The tarball is the only file that is untracked. Naturally, I would do `datalad add-archive-content mytarball.tgz` (as the documentation suggests). I would expect this to do two things: 1. add `mytarball.tgz` to annex; 2. extract `mytarball.tgz` and add the content to annex. \n\nInstead, I get this error\n\n```terminal\nmvdoc@euclid ~/exp/hauntedhouse_mne/singularity (master*) $ datalad add-archive-content hauntedhouse.img.tgz\n[ERROR  ] You better commit all the changes and untracked files first [add_archive_content.py:__call__:235] (RuntimeError)\n```\nWhich doesn't really suggest that I should add the tarball to annex, but I tried to do it anyway:\n`datalad add mytarball.tgz \u0026\u0026 datalad add-archive-content mytarball.tgz`, and that did the trick.\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad plugin wtf`)?\n\n```terminal\nmvdoc@euclid ~/exp/hauntedhouse_mne/singularity (master) $ datalad --version\ndatalad 0.9.1\n```\n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)\n\nI can't live in a world without datalad \u003c3","files":null}]}